;; repr/asm's print level's classes (bin/repr-asm encode-check; doc/asm/AMD64-SURVEY.md "As built: AX2 (third slice)", AXS29 (a)):
;; every CHECK text of test/asm/encode-results-amd64.edn's :text rows that is not met is counted under its :by class, one of these
;; (arbace.asm.amd64.check names the class: the run's output, the reader's refusal, the kind of line the printer does not print,
;; the instruction's class at the encoding level, or a failure). In goi's format. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :intel
  :title "Intel syntax"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the run reads Intel syntax (-x86-asm-syntax=intel) or prints it (-output-asm-variant=1) and the Intel reader refuses the file: none since AX3, which reads Intel and prints it as X86IntelInstPrinter does (the 21,318 texts AX2 classed here are judged); kept for an Intel file the reader refuses"
  :decided "AX1's and AX2's scope (doc/asm/AMD64-SURVEY.md §12); emptied by AX3"}
 {:id :unread
  :title "a file AX1's reader refuses"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the reader refuses the file (test/asm/divergences-read.edn's classes); its CHECK texts follow the read"
  :decided "AX1's classes"}
 {:id :other-target
  :title "a run for another target"
  :kind :by-design
  :why "the run's triple is not an x86 one this check assembles for"
  :decided "AX2's scope"}
 {:id :other-tool
  :title "another tool's output"
  :kind :by-design
  :why "the CHECK prefix reads an object's dump (llvm-objdump, llvm-readobj, -filetype=obj), not llvm-mc's printed text: AX4's objects"
  :decided "AX2's scope"}
 {:id :options
  :title "llvm-mc options that change the instructions"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the run asks for branch alignment, padding, relaxation or SSE-to-AVX conversion, which the check does not apply (since 2026-11-17 a run's --defsym is taken: the print level follows .ifdef, .ifndef, .else and .endif for its names)"
  :decided "AX2's third slice; --defsym taken 2026-11-17 (AXS32 (a)'s part)"}
 {:id :lfi
  :title "the LFI rewriter"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the run's triple (x86_64_lfi) makes llvm-mc rewrite the instructions (X86MCLFIRewriter) before printing"
  :decided "AX2's third slice"}
 {:id :directive
  :title "a line the instruction printer does not print"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the CHECK text is the asm streamer's output for a directive, a label, an assignment (`v = %ecx`) or a data line: its first word is no instruction's mnemonic; the streamer's directives are printed with AX4's objects"
  :decided "AX2's third slice"}
 {:id :comment
  :title "a verbose comment"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the CHECK text is one of llvm-mc's comments after an instruction that the printer does not write: since 2026-11-17 the judge holds a comment's text to the printed lines with their comments (arbace.asm.amd64.print/inst-comment: printOperand's `imm = 0x...` and EmitAnyX86InstComments' masks of PALIGNR, PSHUFD, PUNPCK*, SHUFP*, UNPCK*P* and INSERTPS without a mask, the 119 texts met), a miss beside a commented instruction :mismatch; kept for the other comments (FMA's, the masked and broadcast forms, the other shuffles)"
  :decided "AX2's third slice; narrowed 2026-11-17"}
 {:id :fixup
  :title "a fixup's comment"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the CHECK text is -show-encoding's `fixup A - offset: ..., value: ..., kind: ...` line: the fixup kinds are AX4's"
  :decided "AX2's third slice"}
 {:id :show-inst
  :title "an MCInst dump"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the CHECK text is -show-inst's `<MCInst ...>` line"
  :decided "AX2's third slice"}
 {:id :diagnostic
  :title "a diagnostic's line"
  :kind :by-design
  :why "the CHECK text is a warning or note of a run that is not an error test, or its source echo: the diagnostics are the error level's"
  :decided "AX2's third slice"}
 {:id :apx
  :title "APX (REX2, the EVEX maps 4-7, %r16-31)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the instruction is one the encoding level classes :apx (test/asm/divergences-encode.edn), or the CHECK text names an extended GPR or an APX pseudo prefix: none since AX2's fourth slice, which matches, encodes and prints APX (the 4,245 texts classed here met, and 2,322 more the :directive rule had taken for non-instruction lines, CCMP's, CTEST's, CFCMOV's and SETZU's condition in the mnemonic among them); kept for an APX form the printer does not print"
  :decided "AX2's third slice, after the encoding level's class; emptied by its fourth slice"}
 {:id :local-label
  :title "a directional local label"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the operand names 1f or 1b, which llvm-mc prints as the temporary symbol it made (.Ltmp0, ...): the printer numbers them with the symbol table of AX4"
  :decided "AX2's third slice"}
 {:id :dot
  :title "the location counter"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the operand names `.`, which llvm-mc prints as the temporary symbol it made"
  :decided "AX2's third slice"}
 {:id :unpaired
  :title "a CHECK text with no instruction left"
  :kind :pending
  :why "FileCheck's order leaves no printed instruction for the text: a failure to fix"
  :decided "a failure to fix"}
 {:id :mismatch
  :title "another text"
  :kind :pending
  :why "the printed instructions do not hold the CHECK text where FileCheck looks for it: a failure to fix"
  :decided "a failure to fix"}
 {:id :rejected
  :title "rejected where llvm-mc prints"
  :kind :pending
  :why "the matcher or the encoder rejects the statement the CHECK text is written for: a failure to fix"
  :decided "a failure to fix"}
 {:id :crash
  :title "the printer crashed"
  :kind :pending
  :why "an exception in the printer: a failure to fix"
  :decided "a failure to fix"}
]
